    },
    {
      "narration": "Each era had a dominant reserve currency, and each one was replaced.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-reserve",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · reserve currency"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s3"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The British pound was the global standard for roughly a century, until it wasn't.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "globe",
          "big": "~100 yrs",
          "label": "a typical reign",
          "props": [
            "clock",
            "globe"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s4"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The pound sterling was the world's reserve currency before the dollar.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-sterling",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · pound sterling"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s5"
    },
    {
      "narration": "There's even a built-in trap. To supply the world with your currency, you must run endless deficits.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "ink",
          "line": "A built-in trap",
          "props": [
            "globe",
            "x"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s6"
    },
    {
      "narration": "That contradiction is known as the Triffin dilemma.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-triffin",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · Triffin dilemma"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s7"
    },
    {
      "narration": "No empire ever thinks its money will be dethroned, right up until the day it is.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "ink",
          "line": "Until it isn't",
          "props": [
